    [Test][Misc] Align operator test names and organize single-card suites (#20064)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Organize `singlecard_ops` by the implementation being tested: keep csrc
    operator tests at the root, move local Triton suites into `triton/`, and
    retain companion metadata and graph regressions with their operator.
    Update test commands in the operator documentation.
    
    Rename the following eight files in
    `tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops/` without changing
    their contents:
    
    | Before | After |
    | --- | --- |
    | `test_causal_conv1d_310.py` | `test_causal_conv1d_v310.py` |
    | `test_grouped_matmul_situ_quant_weight_nz.py` |
    `test_grouped_matmul_situ_quant.py` |
    | `test_npu_hc_pre.py` | `test_hc_pre.py` |
    | `test_npu_moe_gating_top_k.py` | `test_moe_gating_top_k.py` |
    | `test_npu_moe_gating_top_k_hash.py` | `test_moe_gating_top_k_hash.py`
    |
    | `test_quant_lightning_indexer.py` |
    `test_quant_lightning_indexer_v2.py` |
    | `test_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_310.py` |
    `test_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_v310.py` |
    | `test_sparse_flash_mla_band.py` | `test_sparse_flash_mla.py` |
    
    Move these five files from the root into `triton/` without changing
    their contents, names, assertions, parameters, or skip conditions:
    
    | File | Collected parameter combinations |
    | --- | ---: |
    | `test_prepare_indexer_indices.py` | 91 |
    | `test_quantize_indexer_query.py` | 45 |
    | `test_kda_state_copy_triton.py` | 20 |
    | `test_glm5next_state_gather_npu.py` | 7 |
    | `test_kda_state_copy_integration.py` | 48 |
    
    Merge all eight cases and their helpers from
    `test_lim_mtp_index_reuse.py` into
    `test_fused_scatter_copy_sparse_flash_attention.py`, retaining their
    original parameters, assertions and hardware conditions. Also retain all
    26 CopySFA metadata/lifecycle cases in the same operator suite. The
    destination now contains 39 cases: five original, eight LIM regressions
    and 26 metadata regressions. Existing A2/A3 hardware guards apply only
    to the native cases, not to the restored metadata cases.
    
    Retain local-kernel regressions and document the explicitly removed
    coverage:
    
    | Source | Retained coverage and intentional removal |
    | --- | --- |
    | `test_copy_conv_state.py` | Move into `triton/`. Retain two original
    direct-copy cases and eight extracted FP16/BF16 layout and graph-copy
    cases. Restore 20 dimension-first convolution adapter combinations that
    exercise local `copy_conv_state` packing/writeback: six first-row,
    twelve decode/graph and two empty-prefill cases. Keep their original
    parameters and assertions, filtered to the relevant layout. Import FLA
    only inside these wrapper tests. The other 38 convolution combinations
    do not reach the local copy path and remain removed. Total: 30 cases. |
    | `test_qfa_c8_paged_layout.py` | Move the complete original file into
    `triton/`, preserving all four A5 QFA/cache-layout comparison
    combinations and all parameters, assertions, and hardware conditions.
    Also retain the two extracted MXFP block-zeroing cases in
    `triton/test_kv_block_zeroer.py` (four cases in that file). Existing
    local K-scale scatter tests remain unchanged. |
    | `test_fused_moe.py` | Keep the four extracted BF16 routed SwiGLU
    shapes and restore the four W8A8 AllGather caller combinations in
    `triton/test_swiglu_quant.py` (16 cases total). Preserve shapes, routing
    parameters, hardware guards and the final output-shape assertion; use
    valid INT8 weights and initialized positive scales. With fusion
    disabled, assert that the MLP calls the real local `swiglu_quant` once
    with valid activation/expert metadata, and check its output/scales
    against the existing numerical reference and tolerances. The original
    eight non-quantized integration combinations remain removed; full MoE
    output numerical accuracy is not established by the shape assertion. |
    | `test_mla_dcp_dim0_stride.py` | Remove 14 external FIA
    layout/causal-attention combinations. |
    | `test_mla_strided_kv_writer_a5.py` | Remove 18 MLA writer adapter
    combinations. |
    | `test_copy_sfa_offload_metadata.py` | Merge all 26 metadata/lifecycle
    combinations and their helpers into
    `test_fused_scatter_copy_sparse_flash_attention.py`, then remove the old
    file. Preserve parameters, assertions and decorators. These regressions
    protect input preparation, layout, graph-buffer and lifecycle contracts
    for local CopySFA/LIM operators; mocked LIM cases do not claim
    native-kernel execution. |
    | `triton/test_mrope.py` | Remove eight combinations that directly test
    the upstream vLLM MRoPE kernel. |
    | `triton/test_trace_replay.py` | Remove four wrapper/upstream-kernel
    replay cases. |
    | `benchmark_kda_state_copy_triton.py` | Remove the manual benchmark,
    which is not collected by pytest by default, and remove its obsolete
    invocation and script-specific instructions from the KDA documentation.
    |
    
    The eight filename alignments and six whole-file moves (including QFA)
    preserve contents. Retain adapters, metadata and binding regressions
    that protect an identified local csrc/Triton operator; remove the
    unrelated external-kernel and generic adapter coverage listed above.
    Keep the existing BGMV Expand/Shrink, Sparse-KV Host, and UVA suites at
    the root with their current names. No operator implementation,
    test-selection logic, CI configuration, 310P suite, or multi-card suite
    is changed.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No model/runtime API change. Commands targeting renamed or relocated
    test files must use the updated paths. Directory-based nightly
    entrypoints remain unchanged. This test/documentation maintenance does
    not require a release-note fragment.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified all eight original filename alignments and the five original
    whole-file moves preserve their Git content and test/decorator ASTs. The
    restored QFA file is byte-identical to its original root version.
    - Compared the moved LIM and CopySFA metadata helpers/tests, plus the
    destination's existing definitions, by AST. Original parameters,
    assertions and decorators are preserved. CopySFA now collects `5 + 8 +
    26 = 39` cases; convolution copy/adapter collects 30; SwiGLU
    direct/caller coverage collects 16.
    - Verified the four extracted SwiGLU shapes and restored caller
    contracts. CPU input/reference checks and 16 invalid-input contract
    checks passed. Actual A2/A5 NPU results are reported separately below;
    CPU checks alone do not establish NPU correctness.
    - After rebasing onto main `ad2dd91fa`, Python syntax checks for all 108
    current files (36 at the root and 72 in `triton/`), Ruff lint/format,
    operator-document Markdownlint and `git diff --check` passed. The
    earlier extraction/rename patch also passed focused codespell, typos,
    forbidden-import, boolean-context-manager and package-init checks.
    - Full `bash format.sh ci` was attempted in an isolated checkout. Local
    hook-environment provisioning has not completed successfully; full
    repository-wide CI remains required. Focused lint/format checks above
    passed.
    - Earlier full-directory validation at commit
    `258f1f83610f94be43786a6bcbb45e678a2cbd3e`, before restoring the 50
    metadata/adapter/caller cases above, covered all 105 files (35 at the
    root and 70 in `triton/`) and collected 2,493 cases per platform. Tests
    ran in four complete-file shards. The suite path remains
    `tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops/`. The following table
    records that earlier run, not a new full-directory run of the restored
    coverage.
    - Both platforms used Python 3.11.10, torch-npu 2.10.0.post7, Triton
    Ascend 3.6.0, CANN 9.2, and vLLM 0.32.0+empty
    (`5df63a7203cdb9328d824a27b682e77c7b9928be`). PyTorch was 2.10.0 on A2
    and 2.10.0+cpu on A5. Existing skip conditions, test parameters, and
    assertions were retained during validation.
    
    | Platform | Host architecture | Passed | Skipped | Validation result |
    | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
    | Ascend A2 | aarch64 | 2,158 | 335 | Passed, including follow-up reruns
    |
    | Ascend A5 | x86_64 | 1,208 | 1,285 | Passed |
    
    After restoring the operator-related regressions, targeted NPU
    validation ran all three changed files with normal repository conftests
    and the same pinned software environment above:
    
    | Current changed file | A2 passed / skipped / failed | A5 passed /
    skipped / failed |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | `test_fused_scatter_copy_sparse_flash_attention.py` | 39 / 0 / 0 | 28
    / 11 / 0 |
    | `triton/test_copy_conv_state.py` | 30 / 0 / 0 | 30 / 0 / 0 |
    | `triton/test_swiglu_quant.py` | 16 / 0 / 0 | 16 / 0 / 0 |
    | Total | 85 / 0 / 0 | 74 / 11 / 0 |
    
    All 50 restored cases passed on both devices. A5's 11 skips are
    pre-existing A2/A3-only native CopySFA guards. Node IDs, per-phase
    reports, JUnit and test hashes were reconciled: no failures, teardown
    errors or unrun cases; all three workers exited 0 on each platform. No
    skip override or operator/conftest edits were used. This was targeted
    validation, not a new full-directory or full-model run. These hardware
    runs preceded the latest rebase onto main `ad2dd91fa`; all three
    targeted test files remain byte-identical to the validated versions. The
    four test files inherited during the earlier rebase were preserved
    unchanged and have not been included in a new local hardware run.
    
    ```bash
    T=tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops
    python -m pytest -sv \
      "$T/test_fused_scatter_copy_sparse_flash_attention.py" \
      "$T/triton/test_copy_conv_state.py" \
      "$T/triton/test_swiglu_quant.py"
    ```
    
